   "evidence": "Definition at Kinematics.lean:158 `K.delta + (2 * K.skewness) \u2022 K.avgMomentum`; only `\u27ean, w\u27eb\u2098 = 0` is proved (252). `\u27eaP, \u0394\u27eb\u2098 = 0` (223) and `\u27eaP, P\u27eb\u2098 = M\u00b2 - t/4` (232) give `\u27eaP, w\u27eb\u2098 = 2\u03be(M\u00b2 - t/4)`, non-zero for `\u03be \u2260 0`. Repo definition of transverse: `LightConeBasis.lean:20-21`, `mem_transverse_iff` used at `Relativity/LightConeBasis.lean:145`.",
   "file": "EpsilonEridani/Particles/Parton/GPD/Kinematics.lean",
   "fix": "Rename to a name describing what it is, e.g. `deltaOrthN` / `deltaAddSkewAvg` (and the three dependent lemmas accordingly), keeping the docstring note that its Minkowski square equals `-\u0394\u22a5\u00b2`.",
   "issue": "`transverseDelta` (`w = \u0394 + 2\u03beP`) is named and documented as \"the transverse momentum transfer\", but it is only orthogonal to `n`: `\u27eaP, w\u27eb\u2098 = 2\u03be(M\u00b2 - t/4) \u2260 0`, and in a light-cone frame `w` keeps a non-zero minus-component (`w\u207b = 4\u03beP\u207b`). The repo already fixes \"transverse\" as the part annihilated by *both* light-cone directions (`Mathematics/LinearAlgebra/BilinearForm/LightConeBasis.lean:20-21`: `v_T = v - v\u207a n\u208a - v\u207b n\u208b` with `n\u208a \u00b7 v_T = n\u208b \u00b7 v_T = 0`), so `w` is not in any `LightConeBasis.transverse`. Only `\u27eaw, w\u27eb\u2098 = -\u0394\u22a5\u00b2` holds, not `w = \u0394\u22a5`; a consumer using `K.transverseDelta` as the transverse transfer (e.g. for an impact-parameter transform) gets a wrong vector. Same misnomer in `transverseDelta_def` (160), `minkowskiProduct_n_transverseDelta_eq_zero` (252), `minkowskiProduct_transverseDelta_self_eq` (258) and the module docstring (32-34).",
   "line": 158
  }
 ],
